* text=auto eol=lf
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
# Deliberately CRLF, preserved exactly regardless of checkout platform — a
# regression fixture proving readText()'s CRLF normalization matters for
# TARGET PROJECT files (e.g. a user's ARCHITECTURE.md saved on Windows),
# not just the suite's own LF-pinned sources.
fixtures/arch-ship-crlf/ARCHITECTURE.md -text

# The eval corpus is hash-bound: a run records the sha256 of its fixture, its
# grader and its own outputs, and eval-verify recomputes those from the files
# on disk. Normalising line endings on commit breaks that binding, because the
# bytes a clone receives are then not the bytes that were hashed. It already
# had: secrets-baked-into-image was authored CRLF and stored LF, so nine runs
# verified on the machine that wrote them and failed on every clean checkout.
# Verbatim storage is the only setting under which the digests mean anything.
eval/** -text
